<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply lowered in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply lowered in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to April 28 partly due to a fall in the number of notes in circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   445.106 (+  1.925)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  16.892 (+  0.441)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.515 (+  0.001)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   23.811 (-  0.002)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	  98.975 (-  2.845)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   458.937 (-  1.736)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
